														<tr valign="top">
															<td width="100%">
															<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
																<tbody>
																	<tr>
																		<td>
																		<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="contentRegion">
																			<tbody>
																				<tr>
																					<td>
																					<p>Hi De,</p>
																					</td>
																				</tr>
																			</tbody>
																		</table>
																		</td>
																	</tr>
																</tbody>
															</table>
															</td>
														</tr>
													</tbody>
												</table>

												<p>The European Astro Pi Challenge is back for the 2026/2027 season, and we’re excited to announce that registration is officially open for both Mission Zero and Mission Space Lab!</p>

												<p>Here is everything you need to know about this year’s updates and key dates.</p>
												</td>
											</tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
									</td>
								</tr>
								<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
									<td class="mobile-plr-20" style="background-color: #ffffff; padding: 50px 60px;">
									<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="Presentation" width="100%">
										<tbody>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td>
												<h1 pardot-region="" style="font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 40px; line-height: 44px; color: #002b3f; text-align: left; letter-spacing: -1.5px;">Mission Zero: Art in Orbit <span style="font-size:28px;">🎨</span></h1>
												</td>
											</tr>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td pardot-region="" style="color: #002b3f; font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 15px; line-height: 18px; text-align: left; Margin-bottom: 10px;">In <a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/mission-zero/4w38g4/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA" style="color:#002b3f;">Mission Zero</a>, young people design nature-inspired pixel art to display for astronauts on board the ISS as they go about their daily tasks. They will learn Python fundamentals—like working with variables—and use the Astro Pi's colour sensor to adapt their artwork dynamically.<br>
												<br>
												What’s new for mentors this year:
												<ul>
													<li>Fresh Inspiration: Explore new starter code examples selected directly from standout 2025/2026 Mission Zero entries.</li>
													<li>Worked Examples: Our Mission Zero project guide now includes two worked examples showing students how to code a static image or build an animated sequence.</li>
													<li>Updated Mentor Guide: Packed with practical classroom resources, troubleshooting tips, and quick fixes for common errors.</li>
												</ul>
												NOTE: You will need a new classroom code for Mission Zero 2026/2027 to take part in this year's challenge. To receive this, simply sign in to the <a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/login/4w38ff/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA" style="color:#002b3f;">Mission Hub.</a></td>
											</tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
									</td>
								</tr>
								<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
									<td class="mobile-plr-20" style="background-color: #eefafd; padding: 50px 60px;">
									<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="Presentation" width="100%">
										<tbody>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td>
												<h1 pardot-region="" style="font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 40px; line-height: 44px; color: #002b3f; text-align: left; letter-spacing: -1.5px;">Mission Space Lab: Real Space Science 🛰️</h1>
												</td>
											</tr>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td pardot-region="" style="color: #002b3f; font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 15px; line-height: 18px; text-align: left; Margin-bottom: 10px;">In <a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/mission-space-lab/4w38g7/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA" style="color:#002b3f;"><strong>Mission Space Lab</strong></a>, teams of 2 to 6 young people tackle a real scientific investigation in space. This year, your teams can design their own original space science experiment or follow one of our ready-made project guides to get started.<br>
												<br>
												Students will write a Python program to log sensor or camera data to a file, with every eligible program guaranteed a 10-minute flight slot on the ISS.</td>
											</tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
									</td>
								</tr>
								<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
									<td class="mobile-plr-20" style="background-color: #ffffff; padding: 50px 60px;">
									<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="Presentation" width="100%">
										<tbody>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td>
												<h1 pardot-region="" style="font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 40px; line-height: 44px; color: #002b3f; text-align: left; letter-spacing: -1.5px;">Testing &amp; Tools:</h1>
												</td>
											</tr>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td pardot-region="" style="color: #002b3f; font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 15px; line-height: 18px; text-align: left; Margin-bottom: 10px;">Mission Space Lab teams can test their code online using the web-based <strong><a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/2026-09-14/4w38gb/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA" style="color:#002b3f;">Astro Pi Replay tool</a></strong>. Teams can access using Chrome, Safari, or Firefox to see real historical ISS sensor data, images, and error logs. Offline testing is also available via the Thonny IDE plugin.</td>
											</tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
									</td>
								</tr>
								<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
									<td class="mobile-plr-20" style="background-color: #eefafd; padding: 50px 60px;">
									<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="Presentation" width="100%">
										<tbody>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td>
												<h1 pardot-region="" style="font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 40px; line-height: 44px; color: #002b3f; text-align: left; letter-spacing: -1.5px;">&nbsp;📅 Key Dates for 2026/27</h1>
												</td>
											</tr>
											<tr pardot-repeatable="" style="">
												<td pardot-region="" style="color: #002b3f; font-family: 'Rubik', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 15px; line-height: 18px; text-align: left; Margin-bottom: 10px;">
												<ul>
													<li>14 September 2026: Mission Zero and Mission Space Lab launch</li>
													<li>1 October 2026, 17:00 (CET) / 16:00 (BST): Getting started with Mission Space Lab. <a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/live-ZcJEgsQXO7g/4w38gf/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA">Join here</a></li>
													<li>22 February 2027 (12:00 CET): Mission Space Lab program submissions close</li>
													<li>22 March 2027: Mission Zero submissions close</li>
													<li>April–May 2027: Approved programs run on board the ISS</li>
													<li>June 2027: Teams receive official data sets and certificates</li>
													<li>June 2027: Exclusive live Q&amp;A for MSL teams with an ESA human space flight expert.</li>
												</ul>
												We can’t wait to see what you and your teams create this year! Head over to <a href="https://www3.raspberrypi.org/e/800983/2026-09-14/4w38gj/2754813312/h/n1Jf5ypOtVnq5004D2I4W7p6fHgUk_YUadvK1lr49uA" style="color:#002b3f;">astro-pi.org</a> to get started.<br>
												<br>
												Best wishes,<br>
												<br>
												Astro Pi Mission Control</td>
											</tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
									</td>
								</tr>
